// Every kind of body's movement numbers (docs/controller.md, "Numbers that are data"; D53,
// D136): the mover (terra_motion::mover) reads a kind's entry by name, and nothing in code
// names a kind. The numbers are stand-ins: today's walker's, Jolt's defaults or the industry's,
// as the doc says; a design answer replaces them.
//
// Each:
//   radius, height, mass     the capsule, m, and how hard it is to shove, kg
//   jog, sprint, swim        its speeds, m/s
//   accel, decel             toward a wished velocity, and back to standing, on the ground, m/s²
//   swim_accel               likewise in water
//   air_control              the fraction of accel it has in the air
//   turn_deg_s               how fast its facing turns toward its way
//   step_height              the highest step it walks up, from the floor it leaves, m
//   slope_limit_deg          the steepest floor it stands on and walks up
//   slope_speed              its speed by the floor's grade along its way: five (deg, factor)
//                            points, downhill negative, straight lines between
//   jump_speed               launch speed, m/s
//   coyote_s                 how long after it walks off an edge a jump is still taken
//   buffer_s                 how long before it lands a jump pressed is kept for the landing
//   stick_m                  how far down it is held to the floor going down a hill or stair
//   predictive_m, padding_m  how far off contacts are gathered, and the gap kept from what
//                            it is swept at (Jolt's 0.1 and 0.02)
//   swim_depth               water deeper than this fraction of its height is swum (D74)
//   float_depth              afloat, this fraction of its height is under the surface
//   water_drag               the water's drag on it, 1/s
//   dive                     a swimmer moving while looking down strokes down at up to this,
//                            m/s, looking straight down; holding jump it rises at it (D478)
//   dive_from_deg            it dives only looking further down than this, deg, so a camera
//                            resting a little under level does not take it under
//   mouth                    where it breathes, a fraction of its height: under water there,
//                            its breath is used (D74)
//   breath_s                 how long its breath lasts under water, s (D478: about 30)
//   breath_back_s            how long at the surface its breath takes to come back from none, s
//   drown_s                  out of breath, how long it takes to drown, s: its health is
//                            taken a share a second
//   fall_onset, fall_fatal   a fall hurts by the speed it meets the floor at along the floor's
//                            normal (D476): not below the onset, all its health at the fatal
//                            speed, by the fall's energy between, m/s; water deep enough to
//                            swim in breaks it. D476's placeholders: 12 (a drop of 4.5 m at
//                            today's gravity of 16) and 25 (19.5 m)
//   push                     Soft or Hard (D479): people push each other softly (two soft
//                            bodies give way and ease apart), monsters hard (any pair with a
//                            hard body is pushed apart at once, each by its share of their mass)
//   core_m                   the core by which it stops another body's move, m: closer than
//                            its capsule is left to the pushes, so a body walking into another
//                            is never stopped dead by it, and never passes through it
//   soft_s                   how long a soft pair's overlap takes to ease to 1/e of itself, s
//                            (a 20 cm overlap is under 1 cm in three of these); a stand-in
//                            for review
//   plant                    how its locomotion clips stand a planted foot (D455): the ball
//                            of the foot within `low_m` of the ground is planted, past
//                            `lifted_m` lifted (a jog's ball stands 5.6-6.5 cm over the root
//                            as it rolls heel to toe; terra_motion::feet::Plant)
{
    "Man": (
        radius: 0.3,
        height: 1.8,
        mass: 75.0,
        jog: 4.3,
        sprint: 7.4,
        swim: 2.0,
        accel: 30.0,
        decel: 40.0,
        swim_accel: 8.0,
        air_control: 0.3,
        turn_deg_s: 720.0,
        step_height: 0.55,
        slope_limit_deg: 50.0,
        slope_speed: ((-45.0, 0.9), (-20.0, 1.0), (0.0, 1.0), (20.0, 0.85), (45.0, 0.6)),
        jump_speed: 6.0,
        coyote_s: 0.1,
        buffer_s: 0.15,
        stick_m: 0.5,
        predictive_m: 0.1,
        padding_m: 0.02,
        swim_depth: 0.7,
        float_depth: 0.75,
        water_drag: 2.0,
        dive: 1.5,
        dive_from_deg: 15.0,
        mouth: 0.92,
        breath_s: 30.0,
        breath_back_s: 4.0,
        drown_s: 10.0,
        fall_onset: 12.0,
        fall_fatal: 25.0,
        push: Soft,
        core_m: 0.05,
        soft_s: 0.05,
        plant: (low_m: 0.075, lifted_m: 0.09),
    ),
}
